# .dockerignore for the EQdyna image build context (pathway item 79).
#
# `.git` IS DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED HERE. `Dockerfile`'s `COPY . /opt/eqdyna`
# ships this checkout's `.git` into the image, and `.github/workflows/
# publish.yml`'s gate step (`python3 testsys/run.py unit regression`, run
# INSIDE the built image) exercises two regression guards that read real
# history from that `.git`:
#   testsys/regression/test_history_table.py       (8 bulk-imported commits)
#   testsys/regression/test_pretag_ci_negative.py  (5 referenced SHAs)
# Excluding `.git` here -- via `.git`, `.git/`, a glob like `.git*`, `**/.git`,
# or a broad wildcard (`*`) left un-negated for `.git` -- reproduces the
# 894cdc1 / v5.16.0 outage in a WORSE form: that incident was a shallow clone
# (fixable with `fetch-depth: 0`); this would be no history at any depth.
# testsys/regression/test_publish_image_fetch_depth.py mechanically pins that
# no pattern below does this -- it is not a comment anyone can quietly drift
# away from.
#
# Everything below is a LOCAL, generated, or session artifact a developer's
# box may carry that the image build does not need. Each entry is checked
# against .gitignore and the live tree, and against what `Dockerfile` and the
# in-image gate (`testsys/run.py unit regression`,
# `testsys/e2e/run_e2e.py --cases test.tpv8 --backends fortran`) actually
# touch after `COPY . /opt/eqdyna`.

# Claude session state -- not part of the repository the image is built from.
.claude/

# Generated e2e run trees. testsys/runlock.py rotates a FIXED path per run:
# `test/` -> `test.prev/`, `test.full/` -> `test.full.prev/`. The gate
# regenerates these itself; a host copy would be a stale snapshot, and
# `install-eqdyna.sh` / the gate never reads a pre-existing one.
test/
test.prev/
test.full/
test.full.prev/
.test.lock
.test.full.lock

# Perf/parity tool-generated case dirs and their per-run locks. The perf tier
# is not part of `run.py unit regression` (the tier the gate actually runs),
# and each dir is rebuilt fresh from the tracked compset when the perf tier
# IS run -- a host copy is exactly the "frozen snapshot that drifts" pattern
# this repo's own papercuts log warns about.
testsys/perf/.perf_case.lock
testsys/perf/.perf_case_tpv29.lock
testsys/perf/.scaling_case.lock
testsys/perf/.numa_case.lock
testsys/perf/perf_case/
testsys/perf/numa_case/
testsys/perf/scaling_case/
testsys/perf/perf_case_tpv29/
testsys/parity/evidence_output/
testsys/parity/probe_case/
src/python/.eqdyna.lock

# Build outputs. `install-eqdyna.sh` (RUN inside the Dockerfile, after this
# COPY) compiles src/fortran/ and creates bin/ fresh, targeting the
# ubuntu:22.04 base image's own toolchain/libc -- a host-built bin/, *.o, or
# *.mod would be for the WRONG environment if copied in instead of rebuilt.
bin/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.mod
src/fortran/*.o
src/fortran/eqdyna
src/fortran/_probe_wedge_mesh
src/fortran/_probe_wedge_kernel

# Fetched SCEC benchmark archive (~1.16 GB of submissions; the tooling that
# reads it lives in tracked scripts/scec/). Only testsys/parity/'s evidence
# scripts and scripts/figures/ touch it -- neither runs in the in-image gate.
scec_archive/

# Misc host/session cruft.
.DS_Store
scratch/
resume_claude.sh
relnotes_v*.md
*.provenance
